chat-gateway vendors the platform-adapter contract from @gamalan/pi-gateway.

Upstream:  @gamalan/pi-gateway
Version:   1.10.1
License:   MIT
Copyright: (c) the pi-gateway authors

Vendored files:
  - src/adapters/base.ts  — the `PlatformAdapter` contract / `BaseAdapter`
                            abstract class. Copied VERBATIM (it is pure: no
                            imports, no side effects).

NOT vendored (deliberately), and why:
  - upstream `index.ts`            — its hub. The dashboard is the hub.
  - upstream `sessions/store.ts`   — SQLite session store. The dashboard
                                     already owns a session registry.
  - upstream `extensions/pi-gateway-ask-user-rpc.ts`
                                   — an rpc-mode hack. Replaced by the
                                     dashboard's PromptBus path.
  - upstream `adapters/discord.ts`  — its transport is the ambient global
                                     `WebSocket` + `fetch`, it derives the bot
                                     id from the token prefix (incorrect), and
                                     its `stop()` leaks a reconnect timer
                                     (`onclose` unconditionally re-arms
                                     `setTimeout(start, 5000)`). This package
                                     implements the SAME contract on `discord.js`
                                     instead (see design.md, "Vendoring").

The MIT license requires this attribution to travel with the derived work.
